                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cc76c7e-2891-3813-8283-2a336c4bf828",
                        "entry_id": "a840b062-c70e-3a9a-bdef-7ff32624f45b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто занимается лужением"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "614a7a18-e4c7-49eb-9128-6d5f6c2b0719",
                                "sense_id": "1cc76c7e-2891-3813-8283-2a336c4bf828",
                                "text": "Нам сейчас трудно представить, насколько большие масштабы имело в начале прошлого века применение медной посуды. Профессия лудильщика была почетной и весьма распространенной."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d27bdd7f-593f-4d1c-b33c-180a809897ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "a840b062-c70e-3a9a-bdef-7ff32624f45b",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cc76c7e-2891-3813-8283-2a336c4bf828",
                        "target_lang_word": "tinsmith",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tinsmith",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db5f5537-bd8b-35b4-b9ca-b60bda36e2a5",
                                        "entry_id": "92d68491-4022-3fe9-a0e9-38566042dbee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who makes or repairs things with tin or similar alloys."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a14cd18-9468-4c53-9a8e-f7f160570c26",
                                                "sense_id": "db5f5537-bd8b-35b4-b9ca-b60bda36e2a5",
                                                "text": "\"Then bring them to me,\" she said. And when the tinsmiths came, bringing with them all their tools in baskets, she inquired, \"Can you straighten out those dents in the Tin Woodman, and bend him back into shape again, and solder him together where he is broken?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eec83531-61fa-4a87-922c-4dafc58cf9af",
                                                "sense_id": "db5f5537-bd8b-35b4-b9ca-b60bda36e2a5",
                                                "text": "A little later this was replaced by a new-fangled naphtha lamp made by a local tinsmith which gave a better light but emitted an evil smell."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f49eb796-c0c4-3a1d-bae9-d6a02b06a6b4",
                                        "entry_id": "92d68491-4022-3fe9-a0e9-38566042dbee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dealer in tin goods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c7b0e14-32b6-4b11-8f8e-1a1cb52f4797",
                        "source_entry_id": "a840b062-c70e-3a9a-bdef-7ff32624f45b",
                        "source_sense_id": "1cc76c7e-2891-3813-8283-2a336c4bf828",
                        "target_lang_word": "tinman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tinman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "758bd393-eecf-37ee-9860-606e3538f15a",
                                        "entry_id": "3e1f1cc9-e8d0-3c37-b980-53e56a316c40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A maker of tinware; a tinsmith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e030fcd-490a-4c51-b3a4-2e24a7a2739f",
                                                "sense_id": "758bd393-eecf-37ee-9860-606e3538f15a",
                                                "text": "He seemed to feel quite at home at the tinman's, although they were hammering and tapping away there all day, but people said that the gudewife put a dish of porridge up in the garret for him every Thursday evening; and it's no wonder that they got on well and became rich when they had a brownie in the house."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bdbc48e-efe3-3840-b625-a0a021e24b46",
                                        "entry_id": "3e1f1cc9-e8d0-3c37-b980-53e56a316c40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dealer in tinware."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tinman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "967a71ad-8382-3b9f-8e9f-75a40c952b63",
                                        "entry_id": "de87263a-9e45-3ad2-bbac-159d35372e57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An uncaring or heartless man; a man lacking, or seeming to lack, feelings, emotions, or concern for others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13bf362b-66e9-3ad2-81c1-5e44f0747b87",
                                        "entry_id": "de87263a-9e45-3ad2-bbac-159d35372e57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A master gene in the fruit fly Drosophila melanogaster, whose absence causes the fly to develop without a heart."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34c17e0c-bed1-42dd-a813-ff359781963c",
                                                "sense_id": "13bf362b-66e9-3ad2-81c1-5e44f0747b87",
                                                "text": "Tinman belongs to a special class of genes. [...] But some genes make proteins that control other genes. Some act like master switches, triggering many different genes to work together to build a structure. Tinman is one such “master gene” for the fruit fly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
